  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Friday)\nIssued at 117 PM CDT SAT OCT 17 2026\n\nStiff north winds will continue to usher in cooler temperatures\nbehind the cold front, as a beautiful weekend remains in store\nfor us. Afternoon highs will remain in the 60s, with overnight\nlows dropping into the low to mid-40s. The aforementioned winds\nwill generally begin to decrease through Sunday, remaining from\nthe N/NW for much of the upcoming week.\n\nBy Monday, temperatures will begin to slightly rebound, as upper-\nlevel ridging slowly starts to build off to our west. Thankfully,\nthis climb will be gradual, with afternoon highs settling into\nthe upper-70s and low-80s by the middle of the week. By\nWednesday, the region will transition into NW flow aloft, as\nridging continues to build to our west, and a deep trough takes\nshape to our east. While this NW flow won't affect high\ntemperatures, it will keep dry air working into the area, with\ndecoupled surface winds overnight. This will result in overnight\nlows continuing to fall into the mid to upper-40s through most of\nthe upcoming week. Little to no rainfall is expected the next\nseven days as well, given the aforementioned lack of deep\nmoisture in the overhead airmass.\n\n/44/",
